Interactive_Interface
HOME PAGE
    >NOT LOGGED IN 
        >>prompt user: sign in or log in
            >>sign in
                >>enter in username and password
                >>search for username in saved database
                >>check password entered against password that is linked to stored username
                >>if valid, change screens to logged in homepage (below)
                >>if invalid, change screens to error messgae
            >>create account
                >>ensure username is UNIQUE, does not already exist in database
                >>link password to username
                >>once password is created, take to sign in screen where user signs in using new username and password
    >ALREADY LOGGED IN
        >>logo and name
        >>toolbar (detailed in header outline)
            >>>options on toolbar (settings, profile, feed, search, driect message (?))
                >>>>you can click on any of these options at any time (this toolbar remains
                    at the bottom of the screen everywhere except the login screen) and when you 
                    click on them it takes you to that screen
SETTINGS 
    >Bring to settings screen, which lists prompts:
        >>preferences dialogue selected
            >>>languages (if selected list languages)
            >>>content preferences 
                >>>if selected, fetch data gathered on the users preferences (this might be something we do when we create the account)
                 >>>display data on a graphical interface. Prompt user to select/deselect topics/preferences
                 >>>Once submitted, overwrite old user preferences with what was selected
                 >>>store updated data under the users data 
            >>>push notifications
                >>Prompt user option to push notifications
                >>if yes, update user data and save
                >>if no, update user data and save
        >>statistics (all just viewing, none of this data is mutable)
            >>>upvotes/downvotes History
            >>>commenting History
            >>>posting history
        >>privacy
            >>if public selected    
                >>remove privacy restrictions on posts
                >>update profile visibility
            >>if private selected
                >>remove non follolwers from viewing posts
                >>update profile visibility
        >>deactivate account
            >>>confirm deactivation prompt
                >>>>IF CONFIRMED, remove account from database, delete all info attatched to username
                >>>>IF NOT CONFRIMED, return back to the general settings screen
    
